      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community’s name honors the early settlers who arrived in the 1800s, when German immigrants farmed the fertile Hegins Valley nearby.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sacramento_pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1830s, Sacramento’s first sawmill on Deep Creek helped supply lumber for the booming anthracite coal industry in Schuylkill County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sacramento_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Masser Family of Companies, founded in 1754, still calls Sacramento home and is Pennsylvania’s largest potato grower and distributor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sacramento_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sacramento’s elevation of about 700 feet places it in a gently rolling landscape where 45% of the surrounding land remains forested.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/sacramento_pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town’s humid continental climate brings cold winters with January lows near 22°F and warm, humid summers averaging 83°F in July.",
